    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for the `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow in this Spring Boot REST app.\n\n**What the feature does:** When a create request includes `birthDate` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`), the owner's age in whole years is computed against its `registrationDate`, and the response carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+). When no birth date is supplied, `ageBand` is absent.\n\n**Changes (following the app's existing OpenAPI + MapStruct + JPA conventions):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema. DTOs regenerate from this at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter, and included it in `toString()`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand` derivation (`formatAgeBand`) computing `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and banding it; returns `null` when either date is absent. `birthDate` itself maps automatically (matching field names) from the request DTO into the entity.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres). Existing `data.sql` inserts name columns explicitly, so they're unaffected.\n\n**Test result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
